<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "The lag indicator in the taskbar tray shows the round-trip latency between your browser and the server, measured every 30 seconds."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_palette}>{dgettext("help_features", "Color Thresholds")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <strong>{dgettext("help_features", "Normal:")}</strong>
  {dgettext("help_features", "Under 200ms — connection is good.")}<br />
  <strong>
    {dgettext("help_features", "Warning (orange):")}
  </strong>
  {dgettext("help_features", "200–499ms — noticeable delay.")}<br />
  <strong>
    {dgettext("help_features", "Critical (red):")}
  </strong>
  {dgettext("help_features", "500ms or more — significant lag.")}<br />
  <strong>
    {dgettext("help_features", "Timeout (?):")}
  </strong>
  {dgettext("help_features", "No response received — connection may be lost.")}
</p>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "A normal reading uses the usual text color. Only the warning, critical and timeout states change color."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tab_control}>{dgettext("help_features", "How It Works")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "The client sends a ping to the server every 30 seconds. The server echoes the timestamp back, and the client calculates the round-trip time. If no response arrives within 10 seconds, a timeout is shown."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_status_signal}>{dgettext("help_features", "Where to Find It")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "In the chat, the reading sits in the taskbar tray, next to a signal icon. Point at it to see the tooltip Round-trip to the server. The value is shown in milliseconds, for example %{example}.",
    example: "84ms"
  )}
</p>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "Right after you connect it shows a dash, because the first measurement is taken after the first 30 seconds. A question mark means the last ping got no answer."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_lightbulb}>{dgettext("help_features", "How to Use the Reading")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_features",
      "If messages feel slow, look at the number first. A high value means the delay is in the network path, not in the chat."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_features",
      "A question mark that stays for a while usually means the connection dropped. The chat tries to reconnect by itself."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_features",
      "The value measures your link to the server only. It does not measure a call between two people."
    )}
  </li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_document_alert}>{dgettext("help_features", "Notes")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "On narrow screens such as phones, the reading is hidden to keep the taskbar short. Measuring continues while the page is open, and stops while the connection is down."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_features", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="feature-status-bar">{dgettext("help_features", "Status Bar")}</.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-connection-states">
    {dgettext("help_features", "Connection States")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-auto-reconnect">
    {dgettext("help_features", "Auto-Reconnect")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-call-quality">
    {dgettext("help_features", "Call Quality")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
